  "question": {
    "text": "<p>What will be the nature of flow of water from a circular tap, when its flow rate increased from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mi>min</mi></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mi>min</mi></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>?</mo></math> The radius of the tap and viscosity of water are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, respectively. (Density of water : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ajx4v",
      "text": "Unsteady to steady flow",
